      "pins": ["REG3.1", "FCC2.11", "FCC2.27", "FCC2.50", "FCC2.75", "FCC2.100", "FCC2.21", "FCC2.20", "NAVC2.19", "NAVC2.32", "NAVC2.48", "NAVC2.64", "NAVC2.12"],
      "nets": ["+3.3V", "+3V3", "unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad11)", "unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad27)", "unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad50)", "unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad75)", "unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad100)", "unconnected-(FCC2-VDDA-Pad21)", "unconnected-(FCC2-VREF+-Pad20)", "unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad19)", "unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad32)", "unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad48)", "unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad64)", "unconnected-(NAVC2-VSSA-Pad12)"],
      "observed": "REG3.1 is on +3.3V, while the MCU decoupling and peripheral connections use a separate +3V3 net. The netlist lists every FCC2 and NAVC2 VDD pin, and FCC2 VDDA/VREF+ and NAVC2 VSSA, as unconnected; neither MCU's VDD pins are on either rail.",
      "expected": "The specified 3.3 V rail supplies both MCUs. Their VDD pins must be connected to the regulated rail, with analog supply/reference and ground pins connected appropriately.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"+3.3V\") ... (node (ref \"REG3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"OUT\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad11)\") ... (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"11\") (pinfunction \"VDD\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad19)\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"19\") (pinfunction \"VDD\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3.3 V LDO (MCUs + sensors) ... produces 3V3 for \"MCUs and Sensors\""
        }
      ],
      "impact": "As netlisted, the regulated output does not feed the MCU supply pins, and the MCU VDD pins are explicitly unconnected. The processors are therefore not powered as intended and the board cannot perform its flight-control functions.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["HSE2", "HSE3", "FCC2", "NAVC2", "R11", "R14"],
      "pins": ["HSE2.1", "HSE2.3", "FCC2.5", "FCC2.37", "FCC2.12", "FCC2.13", "HSE3.1", "HSE3.3", "NAVC2.5", "NAVC2.6"],
      "nets": ["NET0041", "NET0149", "NET0118", "NET0138", "Net-(C19-Pad1)", "Net-(C111-Pad1)", "Net-(FCC2-PH0)", "Net-(NAVC2-PH0)", "Net-(NAVC2-PH1)"],
      "observed": "FCC crystal HSE2 connects to FCC2 PE6 and, through R11, PE7—not the MCU's PH0/PH1 oscillator pins. NAVC crystal HSE3's two oscillator terminals connect to capacitors/resistor nets but neither is connected to NAVC2.",
      "expected": "Each stated 25 MHz HSE crystal should connect to its MCU's external oscillator pins, PH0 and PH1, with the associated oscillator capacitors connected as appropriate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0041\") ... (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\")) (node (ref \"HSE2\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0149\") ... (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"37\") (pinfunction \"PE7\")) (node (ref \"R11\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"Net-(C111-Pad1)\") ... (node (ref \"HSE3\") (pin \"3\")) (node (ref \"R14\") (pin \"2\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "HSE crystal (both MCUs) | ... ABM8G-25.000MHZ-4Y-T3"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Neither MCU has the intended external crystal connection. The FCC crystal is routed to unrelated GPIOs, and the NAVC crystal is not connected to its MCU, preventing use of the specified external clock and potentially disrupting configured clock operation.",
      "confidence": 0.97
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows a critical power-rail/connectivity failure: both MCUs' VDD pins are unconnected, and the regulator output net is distinct from the +3V3 net. It also shows that the external crystals are misconnected or disconnected from their MCU oscillator pins."
}

